{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Both endpoints of this trip were amended after booking: the rider moved the pin to Punggol MRT at 07:12:30 (trip_record.pickup_amended_at) and, in the chat at 07:41:40, asked to change the destination to Terminal 3 rather than Terminal 1, which the trip record shows was amended at 07:41:52. Under POL-RD-05 the POL-RD-01 baseline for this dispute is therefore the optimal route between the AMENDED endpoints - the stored figure amended_optimal_distance_km 24.60 km with amended_optimal_duration_min 31.0 - and not the 21.0 km booked optimal. That re-quote is a stored field and is not to be re-derived by the tribunal.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's 21 km figure, and the trip record's 24.8% deviation_pct, are both measured against the pre-amendment booked optimal of 21.0 km, and both are superseded by the amendment. The derived deviation block on the GPS trace makes the same error: its 5.17 km / 24.62% excess is computed against optimal_distance_km 21.0, the booked figure, so it does not answer the POL-RD-05 question either. On an amended trip the only comparison the policy permits is trace distance against 24.60 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-GPS-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Run that comparison and no deviation is established. The governing trace distance is 26.17 km against an amended optimal of 24.60 km - an excess of 1.57 km, or 6.4% of the amended optimal. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH gates to pass: an excess greater than 20% of optimal (4.92 km on this baseline) AND greater than 0.8 km absolute. 6.4% is nowhere near 20%, so the establishment test fails and no deviation exists on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The distance figure that governs is the trace itself, 26.17 km. POL-RD-01 states that where gps_trace.trace_distance_km and trip_record.actual_distance_km disagree the trace governs, and that the 26.2 km carried on the trip record and billed on the fare breakdown is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement which may NOT be cited for the threshold test. The distinction is small in this case, but it is what makes the comparison safe.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-FARE-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace runs the whole trip from 07:19:20, so its 26.17 km includes the Terminal 1 approach driven BEFORE the dropoff was amended at 07:41:52. POL-RD-05 provides that distance driven before an amendment timestamp is never counted as excess against the driver. The 1.57 km residual therefore overstates the excess rather than understates it, and what is left cannot approach the 4.92 km the 20% gate requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.dropoff_amended_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 'five minutes driving around the airport' is the T3 kerb loop the rider herself caused. The chat log records her request to change to T3 at 07:41:40 and the trip record the dropoff amendment at 07:41:52; the admissibility assessment of the GPS trace records two loops of the T3 departure kerb well inside 380 m of the amended pin, which is what a driver looking for a rider who is not at the kerb does. POL-RD-05 excludes from excess the circling within 400 m of an amended point where the rider was not present, and in any event the whole excess on the amended baseline is only 1.57 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.dropoff_amended_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no billing-integrity defect to refund under POL-RD-09. The fare reconciles to the cent: 3.80 base + 19.65 distance + 9.52 time + 0.80 platform fee = 33.77, with no ERP lines, no surge, no promo discount and no waiting-time fee, and the airport surcharge is correctly 0.00 because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there. Every charge line has a counterpart on the trace, so no standalone pass-through correction is due.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00108", "EV-GPS-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.total_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and has not discharged limb (b) of it: the excess she asserts is measured against the booked optimal that the amendment displaced, and measured against the amended optimal no excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold can be shown. Nothing therefore shifts to the driver, and he is not required to invoke any exculpatory clause at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-GPS-00108", "EV-FARE-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-06 profile check clears the driver. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 402, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established, and in any event the excess on this trip never reaches MATERIAL because it fails the establishment gate first. No conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) and no remedy uplift under POL-RD-06(b) is available on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory is in the pool: EV-ADVIS-00108-01 is MISSING, carries no payload, has weight_multiplier 0.0 and its issue code is MISSING_ARTIFACT. The driver does not invoke POL-RD-03 and asserts no road closure, and none is needed: this case is decided on POL-RD-05, whose re-quote is already stored on the trip record rather than being reconstructed from an advisory.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00108-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome follows from the record. The dispute was filed by the rider, the fare breakdown stands at payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the rider's claim is not supported by the evidence once the amended baseline is applied. Under POL-GEN-03 that is NO_ACTION: the present state stands and the charge is left exactly as it is.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
